{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792948347,"nonce":"nyMEOJ12gsJgPcC/LpHd6E01PeY=","message":"Findings that shape the implementation (mapped 2026-10-25):\n\nFormat. Captured code is per function: bytes, alignment and relocations against anchors, not a system object file. The runtime installs it through the existing install path (define_function_bytes with the module relocations, finalize, publish), so W^X, icache and code memory stay cranelift-jit's, the format is the same on every OS, and an LLVM build from CI is converted to the same form at CI time. Anchors: a function of the snapshot (raw snapshot HirId), its call cell, its entry counter, an OSR helper slot (function, site key), its published-entry slot, its bead id as a value, a runtime symbol by name, a libcall, a global of the snapshot (raw HirId).\n\nHirIds are relocated by a per-process base when the snapshot is decoded (bytecode.rs relocated_by), so anchors carry raw ids and the loader adds the base. Symbol names embed relocated ids and generations and are never used as keys.\n\nLibrary bodies are \"finished\" at run time (boxes::run_function + licm + cse). The boxes pass writes interned::small_int_base() into HIR as an I64 constant, so finished HIR holds a process address. It becomes HirConstant::SymbolAddress (a named runtime symbol plus offset), resolved by each backend and the interpreter, and a relocation in captured code.\n\nThe loader checks before using captured code, and declines it (for the whole snapshot, with a trace) on any mismatch:\n- each function's Cranelift signature at run time equals the captured one (address_taken changes the return convention, plugin signatures change extern signatures);\n- each imported runtime symbol resolves;\n- the code was captured under default settings and no codegen-relevant ZYNTAX_* variable is set: anything not on a short list of known-harmless variables (traces, worker count) declines it;\n- the host has the ISA features the code was compiled for (the target triple's baseline at build time).\n\nCaptured code is compiled with every call through a cell (reloadable calls), probes and entry counters as the runtime would emit them, and the library's HIR stays for interpretation, inlining and promotion; resume points compile at run time from the same body, so site keys agree.\n\nBuild-time caveat already present: the snapshot's HIR is optimised in the build script under whatever ZYNTAX_* pass toggles its environment holds, without rerun-if-env-changed. The capture adds rerun-if-env-changed for the toggles it reads, or refuses to capture under a non-default environment.","files":null}]}